      "writtenOn": "2015-03-13T07:13:14Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "As of today (13 March 2015) the change that allows for multiple remote_ids is not merged. However I am glad to see that the docs are being prepared for that.\nHowever, it\u0027d be better to update section 3. and say that remote_id_attribute should be put in the sections whose names are equal to protocol\u0027s name (those added via OS-FEDERATION api) and the [federation] is the last resort.\n\nIf we have protocols like saml2 and oidc added via OS-FEDERATION api then I\u0027d expect configuration in keystone.conf:\n[saml2]\nremote_id_attribute \u003d Shib-Idntity-Provider\n\n[oidc]\nremote_id_attribute \u003d HTTP_OIDC_ISS\n\n\nLastly, if such sections are not added Keystone will try one last time and query config file looking for attribute in [federation] section.\n\nIt\u0027s unlikely to handle more than one federation protocol, but eventually Keystone is ready for that.",
      "revId": "0093a27b9eae51cf3e02e6c556ed20f9111409b7",
      "serverId": "4a232e18-c5a9-48ee-94c0-e04e7cca6543",
      "unresolved": false
    },
